920	We find that for all three final states, the size of the differential LR asymmetry increases with the increase in $\sqrt{s}$ from the SM prediction (solid black line). In the $U(1)_X$ case, it is governed by different couplings of the left and right-handed fermions with $Z^\prime$, as summarized in Table~\ref{tabASM}.
